    {"type":"text","id":"pat_t","x":40,"y":1458,"width":1560,"height":30,"strokeColor":"#94a3b8","text":"[16] The Permission Ladder: tiers map to rungs — notify, confirm once, always confirm, platform sign-off — but the rung is an exit code the model reads, not a control\n[17] Blast-Radius Gating: classify before the change, by dependents, with a special rule for the component everything else reads from","fontSize":12,"fontFamily":3,"textAlign":"left","verticalAlign":"top","roughness":0,"opacity":100,"lineHeight":1.25,"autoResize":false,"seed":215002},
    {"type":"text","id":"missing","x":40,"y":1506,"width":1560,"height":30,"strokeColor":"#fecaca","text":"deliberately missing: failing closed (one line: exit non-zero for NOT_FOUND) · one table, generated from the other · a derived tier, counted from dependents in the repository\n· enforcement: an exit code is a control only if a harness reads it; here the model does · in the prototype: no impact sentences or change-authority text, a fabricated component set","fontSize":12,"fontFamily":3,"textAlign":"left","verticalAlign":"top","roughness":0,"opacity":100,"lineHeight":1.25,"autoResize":false,"seed":215003}
